  "authoringNote": "Five slots are supplied: the encounter, order, receipt and supplier record and f26i-large v1, a supporting note whose metadata sidecar is committed and whose payload is the output of the pad recipe: exactly 1,048,576 raw UTF-8 bytes, mostly U+00E9 (two bytes and one character each), so it holds far fewer characters than bytes. Size counts payload bytes only, excluding the sidecar, the manifest and the template, so the payload equals the bound and the loader accepts the fixture. The note is available, hash-valid (its contentHash is the SHA-256 of the generated bytes), application/json, a valid supporting-note body and states the case beneficiary name and identifier exactly, so it is bound and usable. R02 passes citing the encounter, order, receipt and note beneficiary pairs (eight). The note title and text map to no evidence field, so the filler adds no clinical fact. The receipt references the order version and is recorded at 2026-09-05T18:40:00Z, after the C06 span 2026-09-03T10:00:00Z to 2026-09-05T12:00:00Z of the date-only order, so R05 passes citing four facts. R04 passes citing six facts. The rest follows the supported packet, checked by hand: the final encounter (2026-08-26) and the final signed order (2026-09-04) both name practitioner identifier SYN-PRAC-0001; the order is after the encounter, on a different date, and within the inclusive C01 bound 2027-02-26; the order item code K0823 equals the case; the named supplier record f26i-supplier-status v1 is usable and states non_exempt, established, no new enrollment, no ownership change and the interval 2026-01-01 to 2026-12-31, which contains the assessment date 2026-10-18. R01 passes citing the seven supplier record facts and the order item code; R03 passes citing the nine order facts. R06 stays manual_review for the qualified clinical reviewer with R06.clinical_review and the five full /clinical/ pointers; it neither blocks nor satisfies readiness and draws no medical necessity conclusion. R07 passes citing the stated LCMP flag false (the null evaluation date supplies no fact); no ATP, specialty, home assessment or proof-of-delivery item is required. R08 passes on the reviewed pack and the supported date. R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. clinicalReviewRequired is true. R09 passes. The state is ready_for_review only because every administrative gate is supported. Quarantine and superseded lists are empty, and every parent affectedDocuments set is empty (C07).",
